# 301 redirect map. Slugs that survived keep their URLs and need no entry here.
#
# Verified 2026-08-10 against the live Squarespace site by two independent
# methods that agreed exactly: its /sitemap.xml (13 published pages) and a full
# internal-link crawl of every one of those pages. Together they enumerate 15
# paths; every one is either preserved below, redirected below, or already
# lives at the same slug on the new site.
#
# Targets carry a trailing slash on purpose. Cloudflare Pages serves the
# directory form canonically and 308s the bare path, so "/services" here would
# make every inbound link a two-hop chain (301 -> /services, 308 -> /services/).
# Re-check with:  curl -sIL -w '%{num_redirects}\n' <url>
#
# Re-verify this file if Eric adds or renames a page in Squarespace before
# cutover.

# --- Pages whose slug changed ---
/counseling-services-offered  /services/  301
/denver-counselor             /about/     301
/contact-counselor            /contact/   301
/affordable-counseling-faqs   /faq/       301

# The "Just Coffee Counseling" offer page; folded into the contact page.
/just-coffee-counseling       /contact/   301

# Squarespace exposes the home page at BOTH / and its page slug, with the slug's
# canonical pointing at the root. Indexed and linked, so it needs a home.
/custom-counseling-llc        /           301

# Squarespace's own 404 page, which it serves with a 200 and lists in its
# sitemap. Google has likely indexed it; send it somewhere real rather than
# letting it become a genuine 404 at cutover.
/404-error                    /           301

# Abandoned Squarespace commerce route. Not in their sitemap, but linked in the
# page chrome, so it is reachable and worth catching.
/cart                         /           301
